llama.cpp
bak
.claude
__pycache__

# Subagent-driven-development scratch (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Harness venv (pypinyin for the corpus/eval tooling)
.venv/

# pyenv venv name, machine-local: this file pinned `rime-copilot` for every
# checkout, and a machine whose venv is named anything else silently fell
# back to the ambient interpreter. Declare dependencies in
# tools/requirements.txt; let each machine name its own environment.
.python-version

# Design records, plans and measurement results. A symlink to the copy in
# iCloud (config/rime-copilot/superpowers-docs), kept OUT of this repository
# on purpose: they quote the corpus verbatim -- real messages, colleagues
# names, internal project names -- and this remote is public. CLAUDE.md's
# "Where the design records live" section has the path and the reasoning.
docs/superpowers

# A cmake configure run from INSIDE the plugin (rather than from the librime
# root) drops these here. That is never a working build -- the plugin cannot be
# built on its own, see CLAUDE.md "What this is" -- but the attempt still leaves
# ~900MB of llama.cpp _deps sitting in the worktree, and this repo has already
# been bitten once by a concurrent session's `git add -A` sweeping up files it
# did not own (CLAUDE.md, "a hazard that only exists once there is more than one
# of these"). Ignore them so the next sweep cannot pick them up.
/build/
/.cache/
